i have strongly welcomed applications  made last month by sweden and finland to  join nato  we are now working  very actively on the next steps in the  accession process  you and i have been in close contact  these past weeks  and over the weekend we both we both  spoke  with president edward  the security concerns of all allies must  be taken into account as a part of the  nato accession process  turkey's concerns are legitimate and  must be addressed  no ally has suffered more at the hands  of terrorists than turkey including  grievous attacks by the terrorist group  pkk  we all agree we must redouble our  efforts in the fight against terrorism  that is why at the summit in madrid  i have convened a special session  devoted to nato's counterterrorism  efforts  and that is also why sweden and you  personally prime minister have taken  concrete steps in recent days  to directly address turkey's concerns  you have already amended swedish law  you have launched new police  investigations against the pkk  and you are currently looking at turkish  exhibitions requests  these concrete steps  represents a paradigm shift in sweden's  approach to terrorism in a more  dangerous and more unpredictable world  we are now working together on an  agreement between sweden  finland and our allied turkey  to further address security concerns  including  around arms exports and the fight  against terrorism  senior officials from turkey  finland and sweden have been meeting at  nato headquarters under my auspices  today  this is the second meeting in a week  i'm also grateful that president adorama  president tinasto and prime minister  anderson have accepted my invitation to  meet together in madrid tomorrow  that will be a further opportunity to  address turkey's concerns  and move forward with nato accession for  finland and sweden  finland and sweden's applications for  nato membership are historic  your membership will boost transatlantic  security as we face the biggest security  crisis since world war ii  all allies recognize this  all have made clear that nato's door  remains open and all allies know that  with you and finland as members  nato will be stronger  so once again thank you for coming thank  you for our meeting and pleased to have  the floor  thank you very much and thank you for  receiving me here at the nato  headquarters on the eve of the summit in  madrid  and it's by now has been four months  since russia launched an unprovoked  illegal and unjustifiable war against  its neighbor  the peaceful and democratic state of  ukraine  but russia has not beaten ukraine  but they hope that we will lose focus  they want the war of attrition  but i told president zielenski last  friday that our support for ukrainian  people should not and will not weaken  over time  because this war is not just a threat  against ukraine  russia's war has created a far more  dangerous reality for europe  including for sweden  and this existential threat to european  security order  will be there for a long time to come  and we must act accordingly  in sweden we're just in the middle of  the biggest build up of swedish defense  capabilities since the 50s  and sweden would reach 2 percent of gdp  as soon as practically possible and by  2028 at the latest  we are right now re-establishing  regiments reinforcing the island of  gotland  reactivating national military service  we are speeding up the defense equipment  procurements and strengthening our cyber  defense and intelligence capabilities  but we know that's not enough  building security requires cooperation  with others  and therefore we conducted a two-month  deliberation involving all parties of  our parliament  and in broad  majority we came to the conclusions that  the best way to protect protect sweden  and the swedish citizens  is not only to be a friend and a partner  but also an ally  in nato  and in may sweden applied for membership  hand in hand with our closest partner  finland  and with