 nato's nato counterterrorism policy  and take active parts in these efforts  our stance regarding pkk is crystal  clear it is less listed as a terror  organization in the european union and  is regarded as such in by sweden  during the last years we have several  times strengthened laws against funding  of terrorism  and sweden's terrorist legislation is  undergoing its biggest overhaul in 30  years  a new and tougher terrorist offenses act  enters into force the 1st of july  with the broaden scope and higher scales  of penalties  moreover  constitutional amendments are being  prepared which would have paved the way  for criminalization or participation in  terrorist organizations  there should be no doubt that sweden  will continue to stand firm alongside  other like-minded countries in the fight  against terrorism  our nato membership will have  implications with respect to export  control of defence materials to all nato  allies  alliance solidarity will be reflected  within our national regulatory framework  one of the issues raised by turkey  concerns sweden's response to turkey's  request for extraditions  these patterns are handled swiftly and  carefully by our legal system in  accordance with european convention on  extradition  sweden is not and will not be a safe  haven for terrorism
 

